# yuuka's configuration. Copy to yuuka.env next to compose.yaml
# (gitignored) and fill in the empty values. The authoritative list, with
# defaults, is the header comment of cmd/yuuka/main.go.

# --- Set by compose.yaml; values here are overridden -------------------------
# YUUKA_DATABASE_URL        the yuuka_app role, from YUUKA_DB_APP_PASSWORD in .env
# YUUKA_DATABASE_OWNER_URL  forced empty: only the migrate service, which does not
#                           read this file, gets the yuuka_owner role
# YUUKA_TRUSTED_PROXIES     the edge network plus YUUKA_EXTRA_TRUSTED_PROXIES
#                           from .env
# YUUKA_WEB_ORIGIN          from .env, shared with Caddy
# YUUKA_DATA_DIR            /var/lib/yuuka, the yuuka-data volume (local raw copy)
# YUUKA_LISTEN              0.0.0.0:31480: every interface of the container's own
#                           network, so a proxy can reach it. Published to the
#                           host only by compose.host-caddy.yaml, and then on
#                           127.0.0.1 alone.

# --- R2 (§2.2) ---------------------------------------------------------------
# S3 endpoint of the Cloudflare account: https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
YUUKA_R2_ENDPOINT=
# Raw bucket and an Object Read & Write token scoped to it. yuuka reads
# raw/ and writes only its sent copies, create-only, under sent/ (§2.2).
YUUKA_R2_RAW_BUCKET=
YUUKA_R2_RAW_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
YUUKA_R2_RAW_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Pending bucket (must differ from the raw one) and a read-write token for it.
YUUKA_R2_PENDING_BUCKET=
YUUKA_R2_PENDING_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
YUUKA_R2_PENDING_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Webhook from the Email Worker (§2.2) -------------------------------------
# Comma-separated, each at least 32 bytes; list two while rotating. Must
# match the Worker's secret. Generate one: openssl rand -hex 32
YUUKA_WEBHOOK_SECRETS=

# --- Ingest ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Name of the Cloudflare account (default cloudflare). Its row in accounts is
# created on first ingest. Redelivery dedupe is per account, so changing the
# name later starts a new account instead of renaming the old one.
YUUKA_ACCOUNT=
# authserv-id of the account's trusted receiver (default mx.cloudflare.net).
YUUKA_TRUSTED_AUTHSERV_ID=
# Period of the pending/ reconcile in serve (default 5m).
YUUKA_RECONCILE_INTERVAL=

# --- Notifications (optional; set both or neither) ---------------------------
YUUKA_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
YUUKA_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- WebUI -------------------------------------------------------------------
# WebAuthn relying party id (default: the host of YUUKA_WEB_ORIGIN). Changing
# it later invalidates every registered passkey.
YUUKA_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=

# --- MCP over stdio ----------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token `yuuka mcp --stdio` acts as. Not needed by serve: agents
# normally reach MCP over HTTPS at /mcp with their own token.
YUUKA_MCP_TOKEN=
